====>       Rule Based Systems

Q): This is a semantic net question, where we represent supersets, subsets and the relations between them as code. We will use the CLIPS IDE to do this.

CLIPS can be downloaded from https://clipsrules.sourceforge.net.

## Tasks

1. Get CLIPS running. It's on https://clipsrules.sourceforge.net. Go to Download; I got CLIPS 6.4.2.
2. Run it, and you get the CLIPS shell.
3. Assert some facts: `(assert (duck))`, then `(facts)`.
4. Make some rules. Open up a file and write `(defrule bob (duck) => (assert (chicken)))`. Load it in and run.
5. Now make some assertions that define a hierarchy of mammals. You can do it in a variety of ways, but I used facts that looked like `(isa canine mammal)`.
6. Make sure that you have some grandchild nodes, like `(isa wolf canine)`.
7. Make a rule which expands the `isa` relation. In my case it added the fact `(isa wolf mammal)`.
8. Now add some feature facts, for example `(feature blood mammal warm)`. Only add them in the appropriate place in the hierarchy (don't also say `(feature blood canine warm)`).
9. Now add a rule which exploits the `isa` relations to put these facts in.
10. If you haven't already done so, add an initial rule that puts your basic facts in the system, reset and see what you get. You should also save your rules into a `.clp` file, clear, reset, load the file, run and see what you get.
11. Now implement overriding inheritance. For instance, by default mammals travel by walking, but bats do not. I did this by modifying my feature inheritance rule.
12. Now add enough nodes so that it expands to over 100 facts. (I did it with 20 facts, but I'm sure I could have used fewer.)

sol:

(deffacts animal-kingdom
   (mammals)

   (isa mammal animal)
   (isa bird animal)
   (isa canine mammal)
   (isa bat mammal)
   (isa whale mammal)
   (isa dog canine)
   (isa wolf canine)
   (isa german-shepherd dog)
   (isa penguin bird)

   (feature blood mammal warm)
   (feature blood bird warm)
   (feature covering mammal hair)
   (feature covering bird feathers)
   (feature movement mammal walk)
   (feature movement bat fly)
   (feature movement whale swim)
   (feature movement bird fly)
   (feature movement penguin swim)

   (instance oscar german-shepherd)
   (instance pingu penguin)
   
   (subclasses canine)
   (features oscar)
)
(defrule expand-isa
   (isa ?child ?parent)
   (isa ?parent ?grandparent)
   =>
   (assert (isa ?child ?grandparent)))

(defrule expand-instance
   (instance ?instance-name ?class-name)
   (isa ?class-name ?ancestor)
   =>
   (assert (instance ?instance-name ?ancestor)))

(defrule inherit-feature
   (isa ?child ?parent)
   (feature ?feature-name ?parent ?feature-value)
   (not (feature ?feature-name ?child ?child-value))
   (not (and (isa ?child ?middle)
             (isa ?middle ?parent)
             (feature ?feature-name ?middle ?middle-value)))
   =>
   (assert (feature ?feature-name ?child ?feature-value)))

(defrule inherit-feature-instance
   (instance ?instance-name ?class-name)
   (feature ?feature-name ?class-name ?feature-value)
   (not (feature ?feature-name ?instance-name ?instance-value))
   (not (and (instance ?instance-name ?middle)
             (isa ?middle ?class-name)
             (feature ?feature-name ?middle ?middle-value)))
   =>
   (assert (feature ?feature-name ?instance-name ?feature-value)))

(defrule print-subclasses
   (subclasses ?animal)
   (isa ?subclass ?animal)
   =>
   (printout t ?subclass " is a kind of " ?animal crlf))

(defrule print-features
   (features ?animal)
   (feature ?feature-name ?animal ?feature-value)
   =>
   (printout t ?animal " = " ?feature-name "= " ?feature-value crlf))
